        "original_id": "164cb5a2-bf6b-55f5-ac94-559a617a84f4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Kristensen, Petter Solberg, David Coulthard, Pascal Wehrlein, Hamble James Leacock\n- Events: 2014 Race of Champions, Nations' Cup, individual contest, 24 Hours of Le Mans\n- Places: Bushy Park, Barbados\n- Topics: motorsport records, birthplace and family background\n\nFacts:\n- Hamble James Leacock was born in Barbados, where his father was a slaveholder.\n- From 2000 to 2005, Tom Kristensen won six consecutive 24 Hours of Le Mans races.\n- Tom Kristensen holds the record for the most wins at the 24 Hours of Le Mans with nine victories.\n- Later in 2014, Bushy Park in Barbados hosted the 2014 Race of Champions.\n- At the 2014 Race of Champions, the Nordic team of Tom Kristensen and Petter Solberg won the Nations' Cup.\n- At the 2014 Race of Champions, David Coulthard won the individual contest by defeating Pascal Wehrlein 2–0 in the final.",
